{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2e3794f01aab746fc7dda899a695426344f9c6c9a78fbc6579a0ba48eafd8831","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"boringcomputers/nehemiah@fea6f0a52991 snapshot 492454999a25ebcf","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6bfacbbb82cf473c528b1ea114a9b3d8606948fcc94de6e90c3347b4410c255d","slc_9ec6fe1c2be48ec60b42715595a7941de2f97833a97a110eee3aa9377f39067f"],"source_ids":["src_6e8b487ed9c85c17a5aa3ee67e177818"],"text":"Managed machines move through persisted lifecycle states (requested, placing, starting, running, stopping, stopped, failed, lost); terminal records never regress, and a machine declared lost is never presented as recovered.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_36e37e49562b2b017ce12be1619d556474c724bd230b1c52a17f99bd2a1ada70","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"boringcomputers/nehemiah@fea6f0a52991 snapshot 492454999a25ebcf","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9e17b25c2abb7ed5817eed64602d081c3fb14d785dd493876736f66e3b3f6c4e","slc_da7400870965a372bb7b53b8de3fb04f477da2d7653fea6173df357a40c6fae5"],"source_ids":["src_98ba94c2a3d259a7b62a3161e96047a2"],"text":"Each machine is a hardware-virtualized Firecracker microVM with its own kernel, jailed and resource-capped, restored from a memory snapshot in milliseconds, with guests network-isolated behind an egress firewall.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca"}
