{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7170227d3bda5cb1fdc4dc7708451a7879aa84ad27d64922ec960c1d430e7bfa","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"boringcomputers/nehemiah@fea6f0a52991 snapshot 492454999a25ebcf","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_29bf78e64335feddba4416f6ca7264be4df4e78a02861e2010dbe09a439a6464","slc_555f1a92f02cca88fddc93fa5dee32ec38dc920aa80c906288543decd6f9dc1a"],"source_ids":["src_98ba94c2a3d259a7b62a3161e96047a2"],"text":"An MCP server package (nehemiah-mcp) lets clients like Claude Desktop and Cursor spin up and drive Nehemiah computers as a tool, configured via npx with a NEHEMIAH_URL env var.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7c6e2a602675cae366b0be89cf922f8135be106869c65a19921311896fa5adf1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"boringcomputers/nehemiah@fea6f0a52991 snapshot 492454999a25ebcf","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_21a4aeab5be883b9defee083ac255e641d84278a9776a26e3b0291237b877c0f","slc_433c99a368a2a1ec32880f7f0ba77974e47aeb31ced24ef34c1e538787ab4e13"],"source_ids":["src_98ba94c2a3d259a7b62a3161e96047a2"],"text":"The repo is a Turborepo/npm-workspaces monorepo: apps/web (SvelteKit site), nehemiahd (Go host daemon), packages/sdk (Effect-native TypeScript client), packages/mcp, and infra/latitude provisioning.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8ce63f73fc921269d564c3fb8a18964c6ca7e74625abbc3e7eb1671dd9146aaa","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"boringcomputers/nehemiah@fea6f0a52991 snapshot 492454999a25ebcf","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5260d21021aa32810e66c3be6904571419ef1351e05e98c3fb5b47c73de4cd4e"],"source_ids":["src_3f90deb4003b5c8e84e129b05844b381"],"text":"Managed host-local LLM agents are not implemented; agent-capability session issuance fails with typed not_supported, and users are directed to run agents inside the guest via exec/TTY/file primitives.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9a76a549662b2421f785e6ccdb42c4f38db9fe766c43ed4b58f73a2b59a93389","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"boringcomputers/nehemiah@fea6f0a52991 snapshot 492454999a25ebcf","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3d70c5508f17ece800491579273a8c5aa4a0437bafd0e827806400d231e09ff1","slc_59feb2542c89afe4ea4143d0fa7d0522b7186b186ff5e09c5dbd7b705c8b0502","slc_d40f5aba64ff32246bcd2dfce9b978da49ea16f32cfee4fc0d579e414435d4dc"],"source_ids":["src_bd14f38d5319510aaa5289cafd1e81ba"],"text":"In local mode the guest shell runs over serial: the kernel boots with console=ttyS0 and nehemiahd pumps the Firecracker child's stdin/stdout as the terminal, working identically for cold-boot and snapshot-restored VMs.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ae6737a936e8bc68260bf5dd36c5888da7c61e3071fb7c20dbde768e804bcf57","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"boringcomputers/nehemiah@fea6f0a52991 snapshot 492454999a25ebcf","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ad65844e4c5dc6b3ae894f9ecc856dcd2f66f5299cb720627a10ca743d98c302","slc_cd1ec195c2a6187c7c8b21676a67c55c1126c6bd204c3dc8ccf8be5eec1e35ca"],"source_ids":["src_bd14f38d5319510aaa5289cafd1e81ba"],"text":"The local daemon exposes a REST API on port 8080 (machine create/list/get/delete, branch, and a /tty WebSocket with binary frames) plus an open /healthz endpoint.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d3919cbdc044126fbc9daea90f000aa2f1855cd501eefc732da80825d116b3a4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"boringcomputers/nehemiah@fea6f0a52991 snapshot 492454999a25ebcf","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_762dd7c72931a6b773244bb796d94501d35b135c6bfa345a239c579727b67b79","slc_fc28d9677c261f7075c7b0af37db4d808a668190b0ea1210e844aa919c758321"],"source_ids":["src_3f90deb4003b5c8e84e129b05844b381"],"text":"File access uses capability-scoped session tokens sent only as bearer headers; query tokens, cookies, and redirects are forbidden, uploads are capped at 16 MiB, and sessions can be revoked with a typed DELETE endpoint.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f730ad3510737a84b75bedd0560736e078d47424bb18529a606e56cb6c785f7c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"boringcomputers/nehemiah@fea6f0a52991 snapshot 492454999a25ebcf","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3080fa9f97cd3223aec0e265048a557e7ff127674974983697863da497d7aa23"],"source_ids":["src_6e8b487ed9c85c17a5aa3ee67e177818"],"text":"The scheduler filters hosts by region, architecture, size, template availability, health, and hard quotas, reserving capacity in one PostgreSQL transaction and preferring hosts with the requested template cached.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca"}
